          "title": "You'll want to know: ಊರು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಊರು (ūru) — \"town\", and in particular one's home town. It is the -ur at the end of place names across the south: Bengaluru, Mysuru."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಿಮ್ಮ ಊರು ಯಾವುದು? (nimma ūru yāvudu?) — \"where is your home town?\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಊರು (ūru) is native Dravidian, one word with Tamil ūr and Telugu ūru (DEDR 752). DEDR 752 notes a Prakrit ūra, \"village\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word hiding in every -uru city name."
